==============================================================================
[1] positive control: does the fire move downwind?
==============================================================================
    1030 fire-days with a centroid step of at least 375 m
    circular mean of (advance bearing - GRIDMET wind direction): 145.3 deg
    resultant length R = 0.146   (0 = no relation, 1 = perfect)
    within +/- 45 deg of that mean: 32 % of fire-days

    The offset sits near 145 deg, so GRIDMET's direction is the
    meteorological convention (the wind it names is where the air comes
    *from*) and the fire runs the other way -- which is the sign the
    measurement is real rather than an indexing artefact.
    shuffling the wind against the fires gives R = 0.070 +/- 0.019; measured R is 4 sigma above that.

